  <!-- Tending across a gate is two capabilities, and they live in different work types.

       The doctor half is a travel-to-work deployment in Doctor. Core's Doctor type runs
       110 DoctorTendEmergency, 100 DoctorTendToHumanlikes, 90 DoctorTendToSelf,
       80 DoctorFeedHumanlikes, 70 DoBillsMedicalHumanOperation, 65 FeedHemogen,
       60 DoctorRescue, 50 DoctorTendToAnimals, 40 DoctorFeedAnimals,
       30 DoBillsMedicalAnimalOperation, 20 TakeToBedToOperate, 10 VisitSickPawn.

       Continuing sits at 102: above routine local tending so a doctor partway to a gate is
       not turned around by an ordinary patient at home, but still below a local EMERGENCY
       (110), which must always win. Starting sits at 5, below every Core doctor giver
       including visiting the sick, so a doctor only crosses when there is no doctoring at
       all on this side.

       The medicine half is a carry, so it is Hauling like the other carries. It outranks
       construction material and bill ingredients on both halves, because a patient needing
       medicine is more urgent than a stalled build or a stalled bench: continue 13 above
       construction's 12 and bills' 11, start 9 above construction's 8 and bills' 7. All stay
       well below Core's HaulGeneral (15) so ordinary local hauling always wins.

       Balance decisions, recorded as such, and player-tunable while the game runs. -->

  <WorkGiverDef>
    <defName>RR_ConnectedTendingContinue</defName>
    <label>travel on to treat a patient through a gate</label>
    <giverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.ConnectedWork.WorkGiver_ConnectedTendingContinue</giverClass>
