  <!-- Rescue in place is the counterpart of the casualty pair below, not a duplicate: that
       one carries our downed home to a bed, this one crosses to tuck them into a bed on the
       far side when there is one there. An injured person taken through a gate is one more
       crossing for somebody who cannot walk.

       Continuing sits at 62, just above Core's DoctorRescue (60), so a rescuer partway to a
       gate is not turned around by a casualty at home that somebody else can reach - but
       still below the medical operation at 70 and all tending above it. Starting sits at 3,
       below every Core doctor giver and below both cross-gate tending (5) and feeding (4),
       because somebody already lying on the floor across a gate is the least time-critical of
       the three once the gate itself is open.

       Balance decisions, recorded as such, and player-tunable while the game runs. -->

  <WorkGiverDef>
    <defName>RR_ConnectedRescueInPlaceContinue</defName>
    <label>travel on to bed a casualty through a gate</label>
    <giverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.ConnectedWork.WorkGiver_ConnectedRescueInPlaceContinue</giverClass>
