  <!-- The three upkeep families share one decisive Core rule: cleaning, repair and
       firefighting only ever happen inside that map's Home area. Core's own givers check
       map.areaManager.Home and refuse otherwise, so a generated Backrooms coordinate with no
       Home area set attracts none of this work - exactly as it attracts none of Core's own.
       Nobody crosses a gate to sweep an anomalous corridor unless the player called it home.

       Cleaning: Core has CleanFilth at 8 in Cleaning, and ClearSnow above it. Continuing at
       22 keeps a traveller moving; starting at 2 sits below every local cleaning job.

       Repair: Core's Construction ladder has Repair at 40. Continuing at 42 edges above it so
       a traveller is not turned around; starting at 3 sits below everything local, just under
       the cross-gate construction-finishing start at 5, because a wall losing hit points is
       less urgent than a half-built one.

       Firefighting: Core's Firefighter type has a single giver. Continuing at 82 keeps a
       traveller going; starting at 2 sits below it, so a fire at home is always fought first.
       Note the crossing itself uses the pawn's own danger policy and never Deadly, so a
       burning map on the far side does not override what the player allowed.

       Balance decisions, recorded as such, and player-tunable while the game runs. -->

  <WorkGiverDef>
    <defName>RR_ConnectedCleaningContinue</defName>
    <label>travel on to clean through a gate</label>
    <giverClass>RimroomsAsyncIndustries.ConnectedWork.WorkGiver_ConnectedCleaningContinue</giverClass>
