  <!-- The fieldwork families answer their candidate question the same way: the player has
       already said, on that map, that this work is wanted. Mining, hunting and plant cutting
       are driven by designations and growing-zone work by a zone, both recorded on the map
       itself, so nothing is ever inferred. If nothing was designated on a Backrooms
       coordinate, nobody crosses a gate to mine, hunt or cut anything there.

       Each work type here has a single Core giver at its own priority, so every one of these
       uses the same pair: continuing at 22 to keep a traveller moving, starting at 2 so any
       local work of the same kind is always preferred. Uniform on purpose - a per-family
       number would imply a judgement that has not been made.

       Balance decisions, recorded as such, and player-tunable while the game runs. -->

